  "comments": "1987 introduced the Gold Britannia series, where one Troy ounce of fine gold was alloyed with copper.<br /><br />\r\nThe 1987 strike was issued in the 4-coin Britannia Gold Proof sets, issue limit: 10,000 (10,000 sales), and individually with issue limit: 2,500 (2,486 sales).<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/612e12fddc325.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/612e12fddc325.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"172\" /></a><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/612e14a28520f.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/612e14a28520f.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"238\" /></a><br />\r\n© The Royal Mint, 1987<br /><br />\r\nThe 1988 strike was issued as part of the 4-coin Britannia Gold Proof sets, issue limit: 6,500 (3,305 sales), and individually with issue limit: 2,000 (626 sales).<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/612e15278f518.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/612e15278f518.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"147\" /></a><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/612e1530e3078.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/612e1530e3078.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"248\" /></a><br />\r\n© The Royal Mint, 1988<br /><br />\r\nThe 1989 strike was issued as part of the 4-coin Britannia Gold Proof sets, issue limit: 2,500 (2,268 sales), and individually with issue limit: 1,000 (328 sales).<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/612e157281d09.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/612e157281d09.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"199\" height=\"146\" /></a><br />\r\n© The Royal Mint, 1989<br /><br />\r\nNote: Proof strikes have initials P.NATHAN and a frosted effect while Bullion strikes have initials NATHAN",
